{"text": "# Incident Report IR-2026-017\n\n**Company:** Larkspur Benefits Administrators, Inc.\n**Prepared by:** Tevita Fonoti, IT Manager, with Granite Peak Managed IT, LLC\n**Status:** Contained. **Severity:** P1. **Privileged draft: prepared at the direction of counsel.**\n**Tracking no.:** IR-2026-017 / insurer claim FRC-CY-0044186 (Front Range Cyber Mutual)\n\n## Summary\n\nOn Monday, October 12, 2026, a claims analyst entered her Microsoft 365 credentials into a fake\nSSO page. The attacker used the mailbox for about 31 hours, set up a forwarding rule, and\ndownloaded one spreadsheet containing enrollment data for **1,204** members of a client plan\n(Cedar Hollow School District), including names, dates of birth and Social Security numbers.\n\n## Timeline (Mountain time)\n\n| When | What |\n|---|---|\n| 10/12 08:47 | Gwendolyn Marsh (`gmarsh`) receives \"Benefits portal re-verification\" email from `it-helpdesk@larkspur-benefits-login.example.net` |\n| 10/12 08:52 | She signs in at `http://larkspur-benefits-login.example.net/sso` from her workstation `LBA-WS-0417` (10.20.14.87, MAC 3C:52:82:1A:9F:D4) and approves an MFA prompt |\n| 10/12 08:55 | First foreign sign-in to her mailbox from 203.0.113.201 |\n| 10/12 09:10 | Inbox rule \"RSS Feeds\" created; forwards anything containing \"invoice\" or \"ACH\" to `acct.review.8841@mailbox.example.org` |\n| 10/13 02:14 | `CHSD_enrollment_2027.xlsx` downloaded from SharePoint via session at 2001:db8:a0b:12f0::7c |\n| 10/13 15:40 | Arjun Bhatnagar in Finance gets an email \"from Gwen\" asking to change a vendor's bank details; he calls her desk instead. She has no idea what he is talking about |\n| 10/13 16:05 | Sessions revoked, password reset, rule removed by T. Fonoti |\n| 10/14 | Laptop serial PF-3KX81W7 re-imaged; Gwen's phone (IMEI 35 693803 564380 9) checked, clean |\n\n## What we know\n\n- Ms. Marsh's password at the time was `Larkspur2026!`, which she also used for the payroll portal. Both changed.\n- The attacker never touched the claims system. VPN logs show nothing from her account outside\n  the office range (RFC 1918 space behind 198.51.100.14).\n- No money moved. Arjun's phone call is the only reason.\n- Ms. Marsh was back from medical leave for one week and had missed the September phishing\n  training. This is context, not blame. Please keep it out of the all-staff summary.\n\n## Notification\n\nCounsel (Rosalind Achterberg-Cole, 303-555-0144, rac@achterbergcole-law.example) advises this is a reportable\nbreach under HIPAA; individual notices are due within 60 days of discovery (45 C.F.R. § 164.404),\nso no later than December 11, 2026. The District's benefits director was told by phone\non October 15. Credit monitoring quote: $14,448 ($12 per member). Policy retention is $25,000.\n\n## Actions\n\n1. Conditional access: block sign-ins from outside the US (done 10/16).\n2. Number-matching MFA for all staff by 11/15/2026. Owner: Tevita.\n3. Remove SSNs from enrollment exports. Owner: Hunter Voss, Client Services.\n4. Shared admin account `lba-admin` still has PIN 4802 on the server room keypad. Change it.", "kind": "Markdown document", "detail": "458 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Tevita Fonoti", "Gwendolyn Marsh", "Arjun Bhatnagar", "Ms. Marsh", "Arjun", "Tevita", "Hunter Voss"], "companies": ["Larkspur Benefits Administrators, Inc.", "Granite Peak Managed IT, LLC", "Front Range Cyber Mutual", "Cedar Hollow School District", "Microsoft", "Achterbergcole-Law"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Cedar Hollow School District", "LBA-WS-0417"], "health": ["medical leave"], "sensitive": ["Social Security numbers", "HIPAA"], "names": ["Tevita", "Gwendolyn", "Arjun", "Rosalind", "Hunter"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 29830.099999997765, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "pass